Z||000000||Flamberge||11-15-2001||01:06 AM||||So I'm driving home from class, its almost 9pm, and this lady in a Toyota-frickin-Corolla starts trying to "race" me. She passes me (as I am going the speed limit) and gets to the light, before getting into my lane. I take her lane, and when she sees this, she gets back over into her lane, so I get back over into mine again. I am thinking "No way am I letting this lady beat me off the line." I'm not really a racing kind of guy, since my Fiero is old, and needs some TLC, but I made an exception for this lady. (Her Corolla was about a 91, beat up. And not a sleeper.) <P>Of course I mow her down at the green, and I kept the pedal down until 5,000 RPM before going into 2nd. It was ugly. So here's my question...<P>Why do people think that a 2 seat car = race? I didn't race her during the first 4 or 5 lights, so why that last one? And what made her think she could beat a Fiero GT?!<P>Anyone else ever been "raced" by someone who had no business even being on the road driving like that?<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||11
