Z||000009||johnt671||11-15-2001||09:16 AM||||Two weeks ago I passed a beat up Dodge mini van on a 4 lane road.  just up ahead was a merge where the road goes down a mountain.  I looked in the rear view mirror and see the van trying to beat me into the merge.  I goose the Fieros gas so he can't pass and then cut me off.  This must have POed the van off because he starts riding my tail.  His next move is to try and get me over to the right far enough to pass me on the two lane.  Then he gave up on that and just tried to pass me.  Every time he did this I just floored the pedal until the van gave up.  The funny part was when he realized he couldn't get buy me he dropped behind me and turned his brites on to blind me.  Only it was broad daylite out.  Jerk!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||87GTZ34||11-15-2001||10:01 AM||||That's a good question...  I get it from off duty police in old cherokees, old men & women in their caddys, beamers etc, young kids in all kinds of cars (rice, parents beaters you name it).  I am not an aggressive driver unless I'm in a hurry but get the challenge all of the time.  Sometimes I oblige, most of the time I don't. I think the reasons they challenge are the the car is sporty looking, the throaty borla exhaust, and 'PONTIAC' light in the tail.  Who knows why but is sure is annoying.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Master_Sushi||11-15-2001||10:31 AM||||Some of you people sounds like really bad drivers. Not leting people pass??? If someone wants to go faster then you LET THEM PASS YOU!! Don't act like an idiot and speed up when they try to. If somebody dosen't let me pass and is playing games I get really mad. I will either illegally pass them on a sholder, or if im in a car I don't car about, I'd probably just push them out of the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> lol.<P>Some people might want to take off faster from a light also, this dosen't allways mean they are trying to "race".||||reg||13
Z||000012||johnt671||11-15-2001||11:49 AM||||You weren't driving a POS red Dodge van ,were you?  This person was trying to pass me in a no passing zone with oncoming traffic.  The safest thing to do was to not let him start to go around me.  If I had let him go he would have gone into oncoming traffic and either hit someone else or me. I chose to not let him get around me.  If it would have been an open road with no one around I would have let him go and been glad to have him far away from me.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
